  "summary_text": "Kyle,\n\nPort Washington held flat yesterday despite Columbus Day headwinds \u2014 that's a win. Grooming revenue dipped 12% but that's calendar-driven; DOW-adjusted performance is only 5.4% behind expectation. The real story: retail exploded (+100%), add-on attach climbed to 95% (vs 61% last week), and your team generated $486 per groomer, above the trailing-30-day baseline of $472. You're running hot operationally. The concern is the month-to-date: you're down 4% in appointments and down 6% in revenue, which isolates to real performance loss once you strip out calendar. Your 12+ week lapse pool (516 dormant and drifting customers worth $318k annually) is the lever \u2014 reactivation focus will move October back to plan.\n\nHicksville is a red flag. Yesterday: zero grooming appointments, zero grooming revenue, all retail. This isn't a holiday dip; it's a capacity crater. You scheduled zero groomers and zero bathers on a Monday. MTD you're running 2.3 groomer-days per day vs 2.7 last month \u2014 that's structural understaffing. Month-to-date you're down only 3% in dollars, but that's because retail is holding. The moment retail normalizes, the gap widens. Fix the groomer schedule immediately.\n\nBoth locations have significant out-of-stock inventory \u2014 20+ items each, with Hicksville's Cannoli at -104 units (critical). Reorder today.\n\n**Capacity & coverage: Port Washington today 6 groomers / 0 bathers; tomorrow 7 groomers / 15 bathers; next 7 days 35 groomer-days. Hicksville today 3 groomers / 0 bathers; tomorrow 4 groomers / 0 bathers; next 7 days 22 groomer-days (understaffed).**"
